WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.410 --> 00:00:08.200
A lot of people are getting worried about
Chinese investment in the United States.

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:13.290
In the first half of 2016, the Chinese spent
about $30 billion buying up American assets.

00:00:13.290 --> 00:00:15.910
One thing people are worried about is are
they buying our technology?

00:00:15.910 --> 00:00:16.910
We could go to war with China.

00:00:16.910 --> 00:00:19.880
Are they taking technology that they could
use against us in a war?

00:00:19.880 --> 00:00:22.189
Another thing they're worried about is the
rule of law.

00:00:22.189 --> 00:00:23.880
Chinese firms obey the Communist Party.

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:25.210
They don't obey the law.

00:00:25.210 --> 00:00:28.110
For example in China, they pollute like crazy
because they can.

00:00:28.110 --> 00:00:29.449
Will they do that here?

00:00:29.449 --> 00:00:31.170
The answer is these are legitimate worries.

00:00:31.170 --> 00:00:34.629
But right now things look pretty good for
selling our assets to China.

00:00:34.629 --> 00:00:38.840
For one thing, $30 billion sounds like a lot,
but the total value of American assets is

00:00:38.840 --> 00:00:41.350
about $90 trillion.

00:00:41.350 --> 00:00:44.850
In terms of technology, we have a government
body called the "Committee on Foreign Investment

00:00:44.850 --> 00:00:48.960
in the United States" whose job it is to make
sure we don't sell advanced technology to

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:50.390
countries that we might go to war with.

00:00:50.390 --> 00:00:53.160
The last one, the rule of law is harder.

00:00:53.160 --> 00:00:55.280
To this point, Chinese firms have obeyed American
law.

00:00:55.280 --> 00:00:56.280
We haven't had big problems.

00:00:56.280 --> 00:00:59.550
You would have heard about them if we did,
but we do have to watch Chinese firms.

00:00:59.550 --> 00:01:01.970
They aren't used to obeying high-quality regulations.

00:01:01.970 --> 00:01:03.300
And we have to make sure that they know that

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:06.900
in the U.S. it's different than being in China.

